- **Retrieval is most of the score.** Without documents `gpt-6-luna` scores {{ floor.answer_score | score }}; {{ better | length }} of the {{ base_tests | length }} retrieving systems score significantly more, the best, `{{ best.system }}`, {{ best.answer_score | score }}.
- **A plain pipeline is the pick.** The top is a statistical tie: `{{ best.system }}` (which rewrites queries with `gpt-6.1-sol`) costs {{ best.avg_cost_per_question | money }} a question, the recommended `{{ rec.winner }}` {{ win.avg_cost_per_question | money }}, {{ "%.0f" | format(best.avg_cost_per_question / win.avg_cost_per_question) }}× less, at {{ win.answer_score | score }}.
- **Agents did not beat it.** `{{ top_recall.system }}` retrieves best (Recall@5 {{ top_recall["retrieval_recall@5"] | score(3) }}, against {{ win["retrieval_recall@5"] | score(3) }}) but answers worse ({{ ast.answer_score | score }}; `iterative_default` {{ it.answer_score | score }}), with a p95 latency of {{ ast.latency_ms_p95 | ms }} against {{ win.latency_ms_p95 | ms }}. Nor did the long context: `full_context_50k` scores {{ fc.answer_score | score }} for {{ fc.avg_cost_per_question | money }} a question.
- **The frameworks' tutorial pipelines retrieve like the built-ins but answer worse.** LangChain, LlamaIndex and Haystack out of the box reach Recall@5 {{ fw | map(attribute="retrieval_recall@5") | min | score(3) }} to {{ fw | map(attribute="retrieval_recall@5") | max | score(3) }} (`hybrid_default`: {{ run.row("hybrid_default")["retrieval_recall@5"] | score(3) }}) and answer scores of {{ fw | map(attribute="answer_score") | min | score }} to {{ fw | map(attribute="answer_score") | max | score }}, at the same retrieval depth and generator. Most of the gap is the null queries: on the {{ run.patterns.questions | dictsort | rejectattr("0", "equalto", "null_query") | map(attribute="1") | sum }} answerable questions they score {{ fw | map(attribute="system") | map("extract", run.patterns.answerable_score) | min | score }} to {{ fw | map(attribute="system") | map("extract", run.patterns.answerable_score) | max | score }} (`hybrid_default`: {{ run.patterns.answerable_score["hybrid_default"] | score }}), on the {{ run.patterns.questions["null_query"] }} null queries {{ fw | map(attribute="system") | map("extract", null_scores) | min | score }} to {{ fw | map(attribute="system") | map("extract", null_scores) | max | score }} (`hybrid_default`: {{ null_scores["hybrid_default"] | score }}): the tutorials' prompts do not make the model say when the passages lack the answer, so it often answers anyway.
- **Two agent harnesses match the recommended pipeline, at {{ "%.0f" | format(cc.avg_cost_per_question / hr_h.avg_cost_per_question) }}× the cost (Claude Code) and probably {{ "%.0f" | format(oc_low / hr_h.avg_cost_per_question) }}–{{ "%.0f" | format(oc_high / hr_h.avg_cost_per_question) }}× ([OpenCode](#opencodes-cost)).** On the same {{ hn }} questions OpenCode (GLM 5.3) scores {{ oc.answer_score | score }} and Claude Code (Haiku 5.5) {{ cc.answer_score | score }} against `hybrid_rerank_default`'s {{ hr_h.answer_score | score }} (Holm p {{ oc_t.p_holm | score(2) }} and {{ cc_t.p_holm | score(2) }}), for {{ oc.avg_cost_per_question | money }} as recorded (OpenRouter probably billed {{ oc_low | money(3) }}–{{ oc_high | money(3) }}) and {{ cc.avg_cost_per_question | money }} a question against {{ hr_h.avg_cost_per_question | money }}, with p95 latencies of {{ oc.latency_ms_p95 | ms }} and {{ cc.latency_ms_p95 | ms }}. Codex scores {{ cx.answer_score | score }} ({{ cx_t.mean_diff | signed }}, Holm p {{ cx_t.p_holm | score(3) }}).
- **GraphRAG does not help here.** `graph_rag_local` scores {{ gl.answer_score | score }}, level with `hybrid_default` ({{ run.row("hybrid_default").answer_score | score }}); `graph_rag_global` scores {{ gg.answer_score | score }}, near the floor: global search reads community summaries, which suit questions about a whole corpus, not a fact spread over two articles.
- **Abstaining is a trade.** `decision_gate_strict` is best on the null queries ({{ null_scores["decision_gate_strict"] | score }}, against {{ null_scores[rec.winner] | score }} for `{{ rec.winner }}`) and the most faithful system ({{ strict.faithfulness | score }}), but it also refuses {{ "%.0f" | format(strict.false_refusal_rate * 100) }}% of the answerable questions (`{{ rec.winner }}`: {{ "%.0f" | format(win.false_refusal_rate * 100) }}%) and scores {{ strict.answer_score | score }} overall.
- **Open-weight generators come close.** Averaged over the three systems of the [model comparison](#open-weight-generators), GLM 5.3 scores {{ mean3("openrouter:z-ai/glm-5.3") }} and MiMo V2.6 Pro {{ mean3("openrouter:xiaomi/mimo-v2.6-pro") }}, against {{ mean3("gpt-6-luna") }} for `gpt-6-luna`; DeepSeek V4.1 Flash scores {{ ds[0] | score }} in `hybrid_rerank_default` but {{ ds[2] | score }} as an agent.

